{
  "id": "22660_keii",
  "headword": "{敬畏|けいい}",
  "reading": "けいい",
  "romaji": "keii",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "awe; reverence; veneration",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "awe; reverence; veneration",
      "explanation": "A feeling of deep respect mixed with wonder or fear, typically directed toward something sacred, powerful, or beyond human understanding."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "22660_keii_ex1",
      "japanese": "{自然|しぜん}に{対|たい}する{敬畏|けいい}の{念|ねん}。",
      "english": "A sense of awe toward nature.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "22660_keii_ex2",
      "japanese": "{村人|むらびと}たちはその{山|やま}を{敬畏|けいい}の{目|め}で{見|み}ていた。",
      "english": "The villagers looked upon the mountain with reverence.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "22660_keii_ex3",
      "japanese": "{命|いのち}の{神秘|しんぴ}に{敬畏|けいい}の{念|ねん}を{抱|いだ}かずにはいられない。",
      "english": "One cannot help but feel a sense of awe at the mystery of life.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A compound of {敬|けい} (respect) and {畏|い} (awe/fear). Combines reverence with a sense of being overwhelmed by something greater than oneself. More literary and elevated than simple respect.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {敬畏|けいい}の{念|ねん}: a feeling of awe/reverence\n- {敬畏|けいい}の{念|ねん}を{抱|いだ}く: to hold a sense of awe\n- {敬畏|けいい}の{対象|たいしょう}: object of reverence\n- {敬畏|けいい}する: to revere\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {敬意|けいい}: respect — a homophone but without the element of awe or fear; more straightforward respect\n- {畏敬|いけい}: awe and respect — same kanji in reverse order with identical meaning; {畏敬|いけい} is slightly more common\n- {崇拝|すうはい}: worship, adoration — stronger, implies devoted worship of a person or deity",
  "schema_version": "2.0",
